          hindi: 'वास्तु-विधान से निर्मित गृह सुखदायक होता है। वायु और प्रकाश से युक्त — आयु और आरोग्य को बढ़ाता है।',
          explanation: 'The Ravana Samhita\'s Vastu section opens with the simplest and most empirically verifiable principle: proper ventilation (vāyu — airflow) and light (prakāśa — natural light) in the built environment directly increase health and lifespan. Vastu Vidya is the Vedic science of harmonious space — the principles governing the orientation, proportions, spatial flow, and material qualities of built environments such that they support rather than undermine the health, relationships, and consciousness of their inhabitants. The Ravana Samhita presents Vastu not as superstition but as applied environmental science: the built environment is not neutral — it continuously affects the body, mood, and relationships of those who inhabit it.',
          science: 'Environmental psychology research on built environment and health (Ulrich; Sternberg; Kellert\'s biophilic design): robust research confirms the direct health effects of natural light, ventilation, spatial proportion, and access to nature in built environments. Ulrich\'s landmark study: patients in hospital rooms with window views of nature recovered significantly faster, required less pain medication, and had fewer complications than those facing blank walls. WELL Building Standard research: optimised natural lighting increases productivity by 18%, reduces absenteeism by 23%, and improves sleep quality. The Ravana Samhita\'s "vāyu-prakāśa" prescription is the most empirically supported element of Vastu.',
          lifeLesson: 'The Ravana Samhita says: your space affects your health and your years. Not as abstract theory — as daily physical reality. Look at the space where you spend the most time: does adequate natural light reach you? Is the air moving? Is there any element of natural beauty — a plant, a view, water, wood? These are not luxuries; they are the minimum conditions for a healthy environment. One practical action: identify the single change that would most improve the space where you work or sleep — better light, better airflow, reducing clutter that blocks movement — and make that change this week.',
          keywords: ['VastuVidya', 'BiophilicDesign', 'NaturalLight', 'VentilationHealth', 'BuiltEnvironment'],
