          transliteration: 'uttaraṃ vā pūrvaṃ dvāraṃ gṛhe saukhyapradaṃ bhavet | dakṣiṇaṃ paścimaṃ dvāraṃ rogaśokapradaṃ smṛtam ||',
          translation: 'A north-facing or east-facing entrance in a house bestows happiness. A south-facing or west-facing entrance is known to bring disease and grief.',
          hindi: 'उत्तर या पूर्व मुखी द्वार गृह में सुख देता है। दक्षिण या पश्चिम मुखी द्वार रोग और शोक देने वाला कहा गया है।',
          explanation: 'The Ravana Samhita\'s directional teaching for house orientation — one of Vastu\'s most specific and testable principles. The reasoning: in the northern hemisphere, east-facing and north-facing entrances maximise morning sunlight entry (the most health-beneficial light spectrum, rich in blue wavelengths that regulate circadian rhythm and boost serotonin) while minimising harsh afternoon/evening western sun (which produces heat, glare, and circadian disruption). South-facing entrances in hot climates receive the most direct solar radiation, increasing heat load and UV exposure. The Ravana Samhita encodes practical solar science in directional prescription — and the reason it has remained culturally persistent is precisely because it works: east and north orientations produce better-lit, better-regulated indoor environments in most contexts.',
          science: 'Chronobiology and morning light research (Roenneberg; Lewy; Viola): morning light (available primarily through east-facing windows) is the most powerful zeitgeber (time-giver) for the human circadian system. Exposure to natural morning light within 30-60 minutes of waking produces: significantly faster circadian entrainment, higher daytime alertness, better night sleep quality, reduced depression scores, and improved metabolic health. Research on directional orientation of workplaces and hospitals confirms that east-facing rooms produce measurably better recovery times and cognitive performance. The Ravana Samhita\'s directional prescriptions encode ancient applied chronobiology.',
          lifeLesson: 'The Ravana Samhita\'s vastu teaching gives a simple daily practice: get morning light. Regardless of the orientation of your home or office — if you can arrange to be in natural light within an hour of waking, your circadian biology will function as it evolved to. This is the single most cost-free, side-effect-free intervention for mood, sleep, energy, and cognition that research has confirmed. The Ravana Samhita encoded it 2000 years ago as east-facing orientation. Your practice: step outside or sit by an east-facing window for ten minutes after waking. Let the light reach your eyes. Everything else in your day will be better for it.',
          keywords: ['VastuOrientation', 'MorningLight', 'CircadianBiology', 'EastFacing', 'Zeitgeber'],
