      summary: 'Volume 4 opens with the Ravana Samhita\'s systematic treatment of Tantra Vidhi — the procedural science of ritual as a technology for consciousness transformation. The section covers diksha (initiation — the transmission of living current from guru to disciple), puja krama (worship as systematic interiorisation of the cosmos), homa (fire ritual as metabolic transformation), and yantra (sacred geometric diagram as crystallised consciousness-map). Ravana was an initiated Tantrika of the highest grade. He mastered the outer forms with extraordinary precision. The section\'s implicit teaching: the inner transformation those forms were designed to produce never fully occurred.',
